NODE_ENV=development
HOST=127.0.0.1
PORT=3100
FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_PATH=/absolute/path/to/serviceAccountKey.json
AUTH_RECOVERY_PEPPER=generate-at-least-32-random-characters
AUTH_COLLECTION_PREFIX=staging_v1
CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000

# Optional; required only when Expo Enhanced Push Security is enabled.
# EXPO_PUSH_ACCESS_TOKEN=replace-with-expo-access-token

# Optional; all six must be set together or the app refuses to start. Enables the Billing
# module (Stripe Checkout for prepaid call/SMS bundles). Without these, /api/v1/billing is
# not mounted at all.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_live_or_sk_test_...
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...
# STRIPE_CHECKOUT_SUCCESS_URL_MOBILE=g000st://checkout/success
# STRIPE_CHECKOUT_CANCEL_URL_MOBILE=g000st://checkout/cancel
# STRIPE_CHECKOUT_SUCCESS_URL_WEB=https://g000st.com/mobile?checkout=success
# STRIPE_CHECKOUT_CANCEL_URL_WEB=https://g000st.com/mobile?checkout=cancel

# Optional; both must be set together. Enables TURN relay credentials for in-app calling when
# a direct peer-to-peer connection fails. Without these, calls still work via public STUN
# whenever a direct connection succeeds, but /api/v1/calling/turn-credential returns 503.
# Works with any TURN server implementing the shared-secret REST scheme (coturn's
# use-auth-secret, or a managed provider that supports the same scheme).
# TURN_URLS=turn:turn.g000st.com:3478,turns:turn.g000st.com:5349
# TURN_SHARED_SECRET=generate-a-long-random-shared-secret

# Optional; all four must be set together. Enables true native ringing for in-app calls even
# while the app is fully killed, via a real APNs VoIP push (iOS). Android needs no separate
# credential here — it reuses the existing Firebase service account for FCM. Without this,
# iOS still rings normally while the app is foregrounded/backgrounded-but-alive; a plain
# notification banner is sent instead of a full native ring when the app is fully killed.
# Get these from Apple Developer: Certificates, Identifiers & Profiles > Keys (create a key
# with the "Apple Push Notifications service (APNs)" capability enabled — a single key
# supports both VoIP and regular push, no separate legacy VoIP certificate needed).
# APNS_VOIP_KEY_ID=ABC123DEFG
# APNS_VOIP_TEAM_ID=DEF456GHIJ
# APNS_VOIP_BUNDLE_ID=com.g000st.app
# APNS_VOIP_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\n...\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----"
# APNS_VOIP_PRODUCTION=false

# Optional; all four must be set together, and require the Billing block above to also be set
# (external usage is debited from the same ledger). Enables the Telephony module (Telnyx —
# outbound-only external calls and SMS via one shared platform number). Without these,
# /api/v1/telephony is not mounted at all.
# Get TELNYX_API_KEY and TELNYX_PUBLIC_KEY from Mission Control Portal > API Keys /
# Keys & Credentials > Public Key (the public key verifies webhook signatures, Ed25519).
# TELNYX_CONNECTION_ID is the Credential Connection tied to the shared number below — the
# client's WebRTC SDK dials directly through this connection (not a server-side Call Control
# dial), so its "Advanced -> Events" option must be enabled for `clientState` to reach
# /telephony/webhooks/calls (needed for billing attribution), and its outbound voice profile
# must allow calling the shared number's caller ID.
# TELNYX_API_KEY=KEY...
# TELNYX_PUBLIC_KEY=base64-encoded-ed25519-public-key
# TELNYX_CONNECTION_ID=1234567890
# TELNYX_SHARED_NUMBER_E164=+15550000000
